  "worked_solution": "Let's call $P(x)$ the given polynomial:\n\n$$\nP(x)=-2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+x+1\n$$\n\nThe degree $(n=3)$ is odd and the leading coefficient $({a}_{3}=-2)$ is negative. Therefore, the polynomial has the following end behavior:\n\n- $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty .$\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nOnly the graph $D$ satisfies these conditions.",
